# Negative Feedback
- Seeks a goal and responds as a consequence of failing to achieve the goal
- It occurs to reduce the change or output
- input signal is the difference between original input and feedback signal
- can reduce discrepancies between desired output signal and actual output signal
	- can minimise errors
- used more in control systems

### Disadvantages
- slower response
- energy loss because of complexity
### Advantages
- good system stability (prevents oscillations)
- system becomes more reliable
- can resist external disturbances; keeps a secure system

### Applications
- temperature control (ex: HVAC)
- cruise/speed control in vehicles
- amplifiers (audio systems)
- dynamic stability (ex: aircraft)
### Transfer Function of Negative Feedback
$$TF=\frac{G}{1+GH}$$

